Upgraded the `hashbrown` crate from 0.15 to 0.17, the `nix` crate from 0.23 to 0.31 and the `base64` crate (used by `stacks-node`) from 0.12 to 0.22, and removed the unused `nix` dependency from `stackslib`. No behavior change is expected.
Rust crates that use the public `hashbrown` maps of `stacks-common` (the `ConsensusEncodable` and `ConsensusDecodable` implementations for `HashMap`) or of `stacks-signer` (`RunLoop::stacks_signers`) must now use `hashbrown` 0.17. Those maps are built without the `raw-entry`, `allocator-api2`, `equivalent` and `serde` features of `hashbrown`.
Upgraded the test-only `rstest` crate from 0.17 to 0.29 and `rstest_reuse` from 0.5 to 0.7. Crates that apply the test templates exported by the `testing` feature of `clarity` (`test_epochs`, `test_clarity_versions`) must now declare `rstest_reuse` as a direct dependency.
